  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Right to a dignified life and sustainable livelihood Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will take place in four countries, Kenya, Malawi, Cote D&#x2019;Ivoire and Ghana is based around a Fairtrade approach called the Women&#x2019;s School of Leadership (WSOL) that aims to build the capacity of participants to be more resilient and empowered. It does so by selecting a group in each country (flower works from Fair Trade producers in Kenya and members of different Fair Trade cooperatives in the remaining countries) and training them on different modules. These modules seek to build capacity of participants on good governance, democracy, participation, market access, transparency and different issues tied to gender equality. There is a strong focus on gender equality; on improving conditions for women and developing better systems in cooperative and farms that strengthen gender equality.  The title of the project is &#x201C;Right to a dignified life and sustainable livelihood Phase II) which highlights that it is a continuation of this WSOL approach from Phase 1 in Kenya, Ghana and Cote D&#x2019;Ivoire. There are also smaller components on youth in Ghana and Cote D&#x2019;Ivoire as well as increasing intra-continental sales of commodities produced on Fair Trade terms</narrative>
  </description>
